Since taking office in August, Colombia's far-right President Abelardo de la Espriella has regularly posted videos that show him walking among body bags supposedly holding the remains of rebel fighters – a communications strategy that has sparked widespread criticism. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa71908-d878-11f1-b19e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2-Colombie-pst-sacs-mortuaires-2septembre.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa71908-d878-11f1-b19e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2-Colombie-pst-sacs-mortuaires-2septembre.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3701a06-dded-11f1-9b12-edf15fb436e4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:52:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>NASA's Voyager 1 phones home from record one light-day away, 49 years after launch</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch</link><description>
The Voyager 1 probe launched by NASA nearly a half century ago has reached a distance from Earth of one light day (more than 26 billion kilometres), the farthest any human artifact has ever ventured from our planet. The space agency received a signal from the spacecraft Thursday, exactly 24 hours after it was sent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667c80bc-e444-11f1-afff-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24166764529324.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667c80bc-e444-11f1-afff-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24166764529324.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ce9cafc-e444-11f1-9311-c9f272e956c0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:26:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667c80bc-e444-11f1-afff-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24166764529324.jpg">© NASA via AP (file image)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump, Xi, Putin summit: What was it all about?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about</link><description>
Donald Trump has left China after a historic first meeting with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Ukraine was discussed without Kyiv or European leaders in the room, which raised eyebrows, though Trump defended dialogue with rivals and Putin said the talks created conditions for future agreements. Xi warned major powers against conflict, and topics included reducing nuclear risks, reforming the UN and increasing energy flows.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2df72-e429-11f1-807c-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-151641-151854-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2df72-e429-11f1-807c-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-151641-151854-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9d845672-e429-11f1-be5b-030c25cd98af</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:12:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
